    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_version_format">Version %1$s</string>
    <string name="about_credit">By TECHTONICPK (Muhammad Riaz Khour, Layyah, Pakistan)</string>
    <string name="about_desc">This app listens to your recitation, follows along word by word, and shows memorization mistakes at once — wrong word, omitted word, added word, skipped passage. Everything happens on this device; audio never leaves it.</string>
    <string name="about_limits">Limit: this app catches word-level mistakes; for fine tajweed, a teacher is final.</string>
    <string name="about_attribution_title">Credit for the original work</string>
    <string name="about_attribution">Engine: Tilawa (@tilawa/core 1.0.0-rc.0, MIT License) by yazinsai — github.com/yazinsai/tilawa\nModel: Tilawa listener model (spliced-clean-lite) — CC BY 4.0\nQuran text: Uthmani text from Tanzil (tanzil.net), reproduced verbatim; phonemization by quran-transcript (MIT); phoneme inventory from muaalem (MIT)\nTraining audio: tlog (CC-BY) and Quranic Universal Ayahs / QUD (CC-BY)\nStreaming Zipformer architecture and ONNX export: k2-fsa icefall (Apache-2.0)\nONNX Runtime (MIT) — on-device inference\nApp code (UI, Android integration, session history) by TECHTONICPK (Muhammad Riaz Khour, Layyah, Pakistan).</string>
    <string name="about_quran_note">The Quran text is the Uthmani text from Tanzil, which this app never alters.</string>
